# TIER 1 - DIAGNOSTIC: band D OptTS with peripheral cap hydrogens frozen
# Purpose: test whether the multi-mode imaginary spectrum of the stall region
# is produced by rotation/bending of the terminal capping Si-H/O-H groups.
# RULES:
#   * Freeze ONLY the peripheral cap H atoms listed below. Replace the
#     placeholder indices with the true 0-BASED indices from the canonical
#     cluster (ORCA counts atoms starting at 0 for the * xyzfile block).
#   * One { C n end } line per atom.
#   * NEVER freeze the Bronsted Al-O(H) proton, the water molecule atoms, or
#     any framework atom of the reacting site.
#   * Diagnosis only: if the mode count collapses to about one, cap floppiness
#     was the noise source and we add the same constraints to all four bands.
# Launch only through cmd:
#   cmd /c "D:\ORCA_6.1.0\orca.exe optts_bandD_frozencaps.inp > optts_bandD_frozencaps.out"

! XTB2 OPTTS FREQ

%geom
  Calc_Hess true
  MaxIter 300
  Constraints
    { C 18 end }   # PLACEHOLDER cap H index, replace with real indices
    { C 19 end }   # PLACEHOLDER
    { C 20 end }   # PLACEHOLDER
    { C 21 end }   # PLACEHOLDER
  end
end

%pal nprocs 1 end

* xyzfile 0 1 neb_ts_bandD_NEB-CI_converged.xyz
